WEBVTT

00:09.100 --> 00:10.640
You don't know when to give up.

00:20.510 --> 00:21.990
Finally.

00:22.350 --> 00:23.550
I want to go home.

00:23.550 --> 00:26.180
Master... Master...

00:26.560 --> 00:28.120
Oh, I'll send you home...

00:29.190 --> 00:30.590
to oblivion!

00:44.440 --> 00:52.780
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

02:05.100 --> 02:10.440
<b>Episode 8 "Meeting the Inhabitants of the Woods"</b>

02:05.700 --> 02:10.190
Sorry for making you look 
after the kids, Mr. Bel.

02:10.190 --> 02:12.710
It's no problem at all.

02:12.710 --> 02:14.130
Hey!

02:14.870 --> 02:16.370
Welcome back, Duncan.

02:16.980 --> 02:18.480
How'd training go?

02:18.860 --> 02:23.960
I'm impressed by the potential I see 
in the youngsters of this village.

02:23.960 --> 02:27.210
They must've had a real good teacher.

02:27.210 --> 02:29.510
Come on, quit it.

02:29.510 --> 02:31.170
Hey, it's Duncan!

02:31.170 --> 02:32.590
You're right!

02:38.950 --> 02:40.260
You're rather popular.

02:40.570 --> 02:44.020
Shame I still haven't figured out 
how to interact with them.

02:44.300 --> 02:47.430
Don't worry. You're fitting right in.

02:48.210 --> 02:51.740
Even if I <i>was</i> surprised when I first met you.

02:52.350 --> 02:55.050
My name is Duncan!

02:55.050 --> 03:00.480
I'm an adventurer traveling the land
 to duel powerful opponents of note.

03:01.310 --> 03:02.230
What?

03:02.710 --> 03:07.760
I've come to witness the 
swordsmanship of the great Red Ogre!

03:08.050 --> 03:11.320
I'm grateful you showed up, Duncan.

03:11.320 --> 03:15.340
Monster sightings have been
 on the rise again lately.

03:15.560 --> 03:19.620
You've got what it takes to live here, Duncan!

03:19.620 --> 03:21.120
Hey, are you listening?

03:20.420 --> 03:23.670
It's true that I've already 
started to put roots down.

03:23.670 --> 03:26.400
Will you settle down and find a wife?

03:26.910 --> 03:29.320
That's not a half bad idea.

03:29.320 --> 03:30.300
Mr. Bel!

03:31.220 --> 03:34.100
A pack of monsters has appeared 
on the outskirts of town!

03:39.300 --> 03:42.270
That's it! Take them down one at a time.

03:43.110 --> 03:45.400
Looks like they've cleaned up most of 'em.

03:45.910 --> 03:48.200
Well done. Nice work.

03:50.060 --> 03:53.080
Do you think I can become 
an adventurer, too?

03:53.080 --> 03:58.500
Maybe, although your dad would be 
sad if you left the village.

04:00.130 --> 04:01.470
Yeah, but...

04:01.740 --> 04:05.000
You've got Duncan and me
 to back you up while you're here,

04:05.000 --> 04:08.230
but as an adventurer, 
you'd really be fighting for your life.

04:08.730 --> 04:12.990
Even if you don't lose your life, 
you might lose a leg like me.

04:12.990 --> 04:15.480
I guess you're right...

04:15.730 --> 04:17.930
Good work today, everyone!

04:17.930 --> 04:19.730
Let's head back to the village.

04:19.730 --> 04:20.470
Yeah!

04:26.130 --> 04:31.750
The parents of youngsters who want to 
become adventurers sure must be conflicted.

04:31.750 --> 04:35.530
I left my own village to become one.

04:36.040 --> 04:37.990
I understand how they feel.

04:39.290 --> 04:41.270
It's a difficult position to be in.

04:41.270 --> 04:44.740
Anyway, those were some 
impressive moves earlier.

04:44.740 --> 04:48.010
I'm amazed you're still honing 
your skills at your age.

04:48.010 --> 04:53.010
You suddenly feel a lot 
older once you reach forty.

04:53.280 --> 05:00.260
You get strangely anxious, like you 
can't keep doing what you're doing.

05:00.820 --> 05:05.780
I know what you're talking about.
I felt old when I turned thirty.

05:05.780 --> 05:09.710
It's a little different from that.
 You feel your age.

05:10.770 --> 05:15.150
Suddenly your body doesn't 
move like it used to.

05:15.690 --> 05:18.670
You can tell you have more gray hair.

05:19.470 --> 05:24.180
They're little things, 
but they make you unbearably sad.

05:24.960 --> 05:26.370
I see.

05:28.080 --> 05:32.170
I am sometimes overcome with sadness,

05:32.770 --> 05:35.940
like I've left something behind.

05:37.380 --> 05:39.020
Like I've left something behind, huh?

05:39.020 --> 05:40.860
Yeah, maybe that's it.

05:41.970 --> 05:44.770
I've tried to live life to the fullest,

05:45.600 --> 05:48.530
but looking back, what have I accomplished?

05:49.440 --> 05:56.330
What are you talking about? 
You raised the Black-Haired Valkyrie.

05:57.340 --> 06:00.000
I see. You're right.

06:00.000 --> 06:04.820
She might be my greatest source of happiness.

06:05.380 --> 06:07.020
Mr. Bel!

06:07.880 --> 06:09.420
What is it, Barnes?

06:09.420 --> 06:12.580
There you are. My dad's calling you.

06:12.580 --> 06:14.840
He says to come to the plaza right away.

06:15.860 --> 06:17.960
Sorry, Duncan, but I've got to go.

06:17.960 --> 06:19.360
Understood.

06:22.540 --> 06:23.470
Kerry.

06:24.390 --> 06:25.780
Did something happen?

06:26.250 --> 06:27.480
That.

06:30.170 --> 06:31.280
An elf?

06:39.820 --> 06:43.010
Welcome to Turnera, good elf.

06:44.010 --> 06:46.960
My name is Belgrieve.

06:46.960 --> 06:50.460
If you don't mind,
 may I ask what brings you here?

06:50.810 --> 06:55.430
Thank you. It would seem 
I've scared the villagers.

06:56.400 --> 06:59.200
They've never seen an elf before.

06:59.660 --> 07:01.690
Forgive them.

07:02.070 --> 07:05.440
No, I apologize for not 
being more considerate.

07:05.740 --> 07:08.160
You're welcome to come to my home.

07:14.910 --> 07:17.350
My name is Duncan.

07:17.350 --> 07:22.460
Once a wandering adventurer,
 I'm now lodging with Mr. Belgrieve.

07:22.720 --> 07:24.970
My name is Graham.

07:25.890 --> 07:28.700
Are you also known as the Paladin?

07:28.700 --> 07:31.710
Some people call me that.

07:33.000 --> 07:35.970
You're a hero who's defeated 
demon kings and dragons.

07:35.970 --> 07:37.970
It's an honor to meet you.

07:38.340 --> 07:41.720
So, Mr. Graham, what brings you
 to these parts?

07:42.080 --> 07:44.260
I'm looking for someone.

07:44.260 --> 07:49.720
While scouring places she may have gone,
 I found my way here.

07:50.050 --> 07:53.250
"She"? You're looking for a woman?

07:53.560 --> 07:56.270
She's a bit of a troublesome tomboy.

07:56.270 --> 07:58.980
She has no regard for her position.

07:59.240 --> 08:01.490
So she's nobility?

08:01.810 --> 08:05.150
Yes. She's one of the daughters of Oberon,

08:05.150 --> 08:07.240
king of the western woods 
in the elven lands.

08:07.720 --> 08:09.460
What's a princess doing here?

08:09.970 --> 08:13.720
Demon kings have been returning 
across the land as of late.

08:13.990 --> 08:17.730
She is on a journey to slay them on her own.

08:18.060 --> 08:22.090
She's slaying them alone?
She must be incredible!

08:22.430 --> 08:26.190
Demon kings possess a special kind of mana.

08:26.190 --> 08:31.100
Only those skilled in its manipulation 
stand a chance against them.

08:32.160 --> 08:35.360
You mean you have to be a mage?

08:35.780 --> 08:37.110
Not quite.

08:37.720 --> 08:41.800
Mana is one direction power can take.

08:41.800 --> 08:45.620
In the old language of the elves,
 we call it ki.

08:46.700 --> 08:49.860
In order to wield a weapon 
as an extension of yourself,

08:49.860 --> 08:54.120
you must use mana as a medium 
to channel your senses to it.

08:54.640 --> 08:58.890
I see. Now that you mention it,
 it is mysterious.

08:59.220 --> 09:04.600
Elves possess far greater mastery 
over mana than humans.

09:05.100 --> 09:08.660
Even for our kind,
 she is exceptionally talented.

09:09.280 --> 09:13.140
But that worked against her, 
and she left the woods.

09:13.700 --> 09:18.170
She believes she's defeating them, 
but demon kings are immortal.

09:18.750 --> 09:21.770
If you followed the princess's trail here,

09:21.770 --> 09:27.670
then monsters must be appearing 
around Turnera because...

09:28.140 --> 09:33.190
I can't say for certain that the rise
 in monsters is due to a demon king,

09:33.190 --> 09:35.420
but it's likely.

09:36.370 --> 09:38.170
Well, that's not good.

09:38.670 --> 09:40.610
We'll need to investigate.

09:44.680 --> 09:46.270
Find anything?

09:47.990 --> 09:50.020
The mana here is strange.

09:50.760 --> 09:54.530
But whatever's causing it is in the forest.

09:55.090 --> 09:58.020
Is it possible the forest 
has turned into a dungeon?

09:58.530 --> 10:01.040
If that were the cause,

10:01.430 --> 10:05.530
the trees would be twisted 
and life itself distorted.

10:05.920 --> 10:10.280
Though the quality of this mana certainly
 feels similar to that of a demon king.

10:28.130 --> 10:30.570
You're both quite skilled.

10:30.830 --> 10:34.400
What are you talking about? 
Next to you, we're practically babes.

10:34.400 --> 10:37.580
Despite your wide swings, 
your attacks are sharp.

10:39.700 --> 10:42.320
This blade is a living thing.

10:45.100 --> 10:50.000
Far to the east, there is a strange 
variety of tree known as the steel tree.

10:50.000 --> 10:53.980
Its fruit is of superlative quality, 
but it is difficult to work.

10:53.980 --> 11:00.330
When forged into a weapon,
 it is especially receptive to its wielder.

11:00.330 --> 11:03.700
Living metal? I'm amazed.

11:03.700 --> 11:07.420
I bet we'll have this little problem 
cleaned up in no time.

11:07.420 --> 11:08.950
About that...

11:10.230 --> 11:15.290
I guarantee she'll detect this 
forest's mana and show up here.

11:15.290 --> 11:17.650
If anything happens, 
I'll do my best to handle it.

11:17.990 --> 11:20.940
So would you be willing to wait a while?

11:21.290 --> 11:26.320
Very well. With your strength on our side,
 we have nothing to worry about.

11:26.320 --> 11:30.010
You're welcome to stay with 
me while you're here.

11:30.230 --> 11:32.320
Thank you for all your help with everything.

11:32.320 --> 11:37.210
I'll never catch that unruly 
girl unless I ambush her.

11:41.490 --> 11:44.680
I haven't gotten enough dad time recently.

11:44.680 --> 11:48.010
He must be missing me, too.

11:48.010 --> 11:50.520
It sounds like the village depends on him.

11:50.520 --> 11:52.380
He might not have time to miss you.

11:52.380 --> 11:53.900
Let's come back soon.

11:53.900 --> 11:54.510
Sure.

11:55.280 --> 11:56.260
Where to next?

11:56.570 --> 11:58.900
Ange, why don't you find a boyfriend?

11:59.400 --> 12:00.560
Why?

12:00.560 --> 12:03.980
If you had one here, you could 
distract yourself from your loneliness.

12:03.980 --> 12:08.750
What I want from my dad isn't the 
same as what I'd want from a lover.

12:08.750 --> 12:10.590
What about you, Miri?

12:10.590 --> 12:14.830
Oh, please. I don't trust men my age.

12:14.830 --> 12:17.240
Don't you think your standards are too high?

12:17.960 --> 12:22.010
I wonder of Mr. Bel would get married.

12:22.950 --> 12:24.240
Where did that come from?

12:24.240 --> 12:28.180
If he had a wife, he wouldn't 
be lonely in Turnera.

12:28.880 --> 12:31.750
What kind of woman do you
 think would be good?

12:33.750 --> 12:36.520
She'd need to be motherly, I guess.

12:37.600 --> 12:39.760
Motherly, huh?

12:40.490 --> 12:45.070
<i>My dad's wife would be my mom.</i>

12:45.560 --> 12:48.960
<i>My mom... That has a nice ring to it!</i>

12:50.460 --> 12:53.390
I'll have to find a wife for my dad.

12:53.390 --> 12:53.950
What?

12:53.950 --> 12:55.790
Wow, that sounds fun!

12:56.820 --> 13:01.660
My dad's a late bloomer, so if we leave
 it to him, he'll never find someone.

13:01.660 --> 13:05.340
So we have to find suitable 
candidates for him.

13:05.340 --> 13:08.700
The ultimate decision will be his, of course.

13:09.550 --> 13:11.670
This is starting to sound like fun.

13:11.670 --> 13:17.190
What if he stops spending time 
with you once he gets married?

13:19.640 --> 13:21.080
What am I going to do?

13:21.080 --> 13:23.310
You hadn't considered that?

13:23.640 --> 13:26.090
No, my dad isn't that kind of man!

13:26.090 --> 13:30.410
So I'm going to find him a wife! 
I'll find my own mother!

13:30.410 --> 13:31.780
Let's get to it!

13:32.060 --> 13:32.950
Huh?

13:32.950 --> 13:34.450
We're going with you?

13:39.270 --> 13:41.250
What are we doing here?

13:43.030 --> 13:44.880
See you later.

13:44.880 --> 13:47.060
Oh, Ange.

13:50.100 --> 13:56.640
<i>I only met Ms. Yuri recently, but her 
skin is unbelievable for a 37-year-old.</i>

13:56.640 --> 13:59.810
<i>She's calm but a bit mischievous. 
She's a lovely lady.</i>

13:59.810 --> 14:02.590
<i>I wouldn't mind having Ms. Yuri for a mom.</i>

14:04.100 --> 14:05.570
What is it?

14:05.570 --> 14:08.770
Ms. Yuri, would you like me 
to set you up with my dad?

14:08.770 --> 14:09.330
What?

14:09.330 --> 14:10.190
What?!

14:10.540 --> 14:15.640
Um, isn't your father the Red Ogre?

14:15.640 --> 14:18.450
I'm not sure I'd be a good match for him.

14:18.450 --> 14:20.080
Oh, don't say that!

14:20.080 --> 14:23.060
You were Triple A-rank, weren't you?

14:23.490 --> 14:26.950
B-Back when I was still adventuring.

14:27.290 --> 14:30.520
Yuri, about this file...

14:30.520 --> 14:32.220
Oh, Ms. Ange.

14:32.220 --> 14:34.700
Not getting enough sleep, Guild Master?

14:34.700 --> 14:38.920
Not really. Staying up all night
 at my age is rough.

14:38.920 --> 14:43.090
It's been like this ever since 
that monster infestation.

14:43.090 --> 14:45.230
All you do is complain, Leo.

14:45.230 --> 14:47.120
Don't be ridiculous.

14:47.120 --> 14:49.530
I'd die if I couldn't complain.

14:49.530 --> 14:53.520
You'll be fine. You're still good to go
 if you can joke about dying.

14:53.520 --> 14:56.710
Here, I'll even check this file for you.

14:59.120 --> 15:03.540
<i>These two used to be party 
members. They're quite close.</i>

15:03.810 --> 15:04.600
Hey.

15:05.100 --> 15:06.660
What is it, Ms. Ange?

15:06.660 --> 15:08.470
Are you two dating?

15:09.130 --> 15:10.140
Why?

15:10.140 --> 15:13.310
You're close. And you trust each other, right?

15:16.520 --> 15:19.820
Well, we used to watch 
each other's backs and all.

15:19.820 --> 15:22.220
But that doesn't make us lovers.

15:22.650 --> 15:26.010
It's less that I trust him and more 
that I feel compelled to help him.

15:26.010 --> 15:26.820
What?

15:27.230 --> 15:31.820
<i>Regardless, a strong bond has 
formed between them. But...</i>

15:32.080 --> 15:36.500
Ms. Yuri, please give some serious 
thought to meeting my dad.

15:36.500 --> 15:39.240
Unlike the guild master, 
he's actually dependable.

15:40.570 --> 15:42.830
My, you precocious girl.

15:42.830 --> 15:45.350
I bet he really is dependable.

15:45.350 --> 15:50.210
I know, Yuri! You should marry Ms. Ange's dad
 and bring him back to Orphen.

15:50.940 --> 15:52.630
I should <i>what?!</i>

15:54.570 --> 15:57.400
But it's a great idea...

15:58.070 --> 16:03.260
<i>If Ms. Yuri were my mom,
would she get that mad at me?</i>

16:03.260 --> 16:04.350
Ange.

16:04.350 --> 16:06.780
There's someplace we want to go after this.

16:06.780 --> 16:08.270
What? Where?

16:08.270 --> 16:10.220
Our home.

16:11.630 --> 16:13.120
We're back!

16:14.280 --> 16:15.780
Welcome back.

16:16.180 --> 16:17.980
How have you been?

16:17.980 --> 16:19.840
Welcome home!

16:19.840 --> 16:21.790
We missed you!

16:19.990 --> 16:21.790
I'll leave this for you here.

16:20.450 --> 16:21.790
How is everyone?

16:22.100 --> 16:24.790
Thank you. What magnificent vegetables.

16:22.570 --> 16:24.790
Ange came, too!

16:24.790 --> 16:28.290
I'll boil these tonight and make pasta.

16:31.310 --> 16:33.240
I chopped my veggies!

16:33.240 --> 16:34.390
Me, too!

16:34.390 --> 16:35.930
Why, thank you.

16:35.930 --> 16:38.310
Could you set the table next?

16:38.310 --> 16:39.320
Okay!

16:40.820 --> 16:45.960
<i>Ms. Rosetta is a sister at the 
orphanage Ane and Miri are from.</i>

16:45.960 --> 16:47.830
<i>She's spirited and good with kids.</i>

16:47.830 --> 16:50.380
<i>She's a very kind 29-year-old.</i>

16:50.810 --> 16:51.820
Hm?

16:52.140 --> 16:54.740
Ms. Rosetta, have you considered marriage?

16:54.740 --> 16:57.370
Wh-What? Where did this come from?

16:57.370 --> 17:00.720
You're cute, hardworking, and a good cook.

17:00.720 --> 17:02.960
You'd make a good wife.

17:03.660 --> 17:06.450
Don't poke fun at adults.

17:07.280 --> 17:09.920
Hey, want me to set you up with my dad?

17:09.920 --> 17:12.620
Wh-What are you talking about?

17:12.620 --> 17:13.510
No?

17:14.030 --> 17:16.710
Th-That's not the issue here.

17:17.470 --> 17:20.970
Think about it. My dad's a great guy.

17:26.240 --> 17:28.740
Rosetta, why are you blushing?

17:28.740 --> 17:31.240
N-No reason.

17:36.120 --> 17:39.740
Sorry. We're still not done shearing.

17:39.740 --> 17:43.110
Don't you worry. Leave it to us.

17:43.110 --> 17:44.580
Thank you.

17:44.580 --> 17:46.080
Well then, we shall return soon.

17:54.760 --> 17:57.660
Good grief. What a busy year we're having.

17:57.660 --> 18:01.020
It's just until the youngsters 
get used to the work.

18:01.020 --> 18:05.760
Say, Bel, do you think
 Mr. Graham likes this place?

18:05.760 --> 18:07.770
Yeah, I think he does.

18:07.770 --> 18:11.510
It's pretty great that an elf 
likes our village, don't you think?

18:11.510 --> 18:15.950
And yet you're still too embarrassed 
to have a real conversation with him.

18:15.950 --> 18:19.660
But I don't know what to talk about.

18:20.740 --> 18:23.030
Small talk would be fine.

18:23.030 --> 18:26.390
Then I'll invite him to drink with us.

18:26.390 --> 18:27.790
You'd better bring him.

18:28.440 --> 18:31.400
You got it. I'm sure he'll be delighted.

18:31.400 --> 18:32.760
Mr. Bel!

18:33.040 --> 18:35.790
Could you come to the far field?

18:35.790 --> 18:38.180
What's wrong? Is it monsters again?

18:38.180 --> 18:40.670
Well, actually...

18:50.280 --> 18:52.640
How dare they flee after seeing my face.

18:52.640 --> 18:54.700
Humans are so rude.

18:55.070 --> 18:59.030
I'm sorry. They're not used to elves.

18:59.030 --> 19:00.420
Forgive them.

19:00.710 --> 19:02.740
So, who are you?

19:02.740 --> 19:05.330
My name is Belgrieve.

19:05.330 --> 19:08.990
Are you the daughter of Oberon, 
king of the west?

19:13.280 --> 19:15.450
I thought so.

19:15.810 --> 19:19.540
Who told you that? Tell me, or else!

19:24.680 --> 19:27.850
I was just thinking about having lunch.

19:27.850 --> 19:29.390
If it's not an imposition,

19:29.390 --> 19:33.150
I'd be much obliged for the honor
of dining with an elven princess.

19:34.440 --> 19:37.150
If you insist, then I suppose I must.

19:37.990 --> 19:39.640
Thank you.

19:51.850 --> 19:53.500
Did you like it?

19:54.180 --> 19:56.510
I-It was all right.

19:56.800 --> 20:00.160
If you don't mind, may I ask your name?

20:00.160 --> 20:04.000
First things first, old man. 
How did you know who I am?

20:04.260 --> 20:06.760
I heard from Mr. Graham.

20:06.760 --> 20:08.760
He's actually in this village now.

20:10.430 --> 20:13.870
M-My granduncle? You can't be serious!

20:13.870 --> 20:14.990
Marguerite.

20:19.300 --> 20:21.530
G-Granduncle?

20:21.800 --> 20:25.150
What do you think you're doing?
 Oberon is worried.

20:25.760 --> 20:27.630
My father, caring about me?

20:27.630 --> 20:29.320
Impossible!

20:29.320 --> 20:31.620
All parents care for their children.

20:31.620 --> 20:33.410
You can't be serious!

20:33.410 --> 20:36.370
I'll make him acknowledge me

20:36.370 --> 20:39.100
the same way you became famous!

20:43.840 --> 20:45.480
No matter how she begged,

20:45.480 --> 20:48.340
I never should've told her about my travels.

20:48.340 --> 20:50.640
She's a relative of yours?

20:50.640 --> 20:54.390
Yes. Oberon is my nephew.

20:56.530 --> 20:57.950
I must go after her.

20:57.950 --> 20:59.660
Then I'll go with you.

20:59.660 --> 21:03.660
I couldn't bear to have you witness 
any more of our family squabbles.

21:06.220 --> 21:09.090
Doesn't sound like this is going to be easy.

21:09.090 --> 21:10.170
No.

21:14.980 --> 21:19.260
Nobody's giving me the time of day 
even though my dad's a great guy.

21:19.580 --> 21:22.000
You're being a bit too pushy.

21:22.000 --> 21:25.570
Yeah, yeah. You're really rushing things.

21:25.570 --> 21:27.250
You think so?

21:27.250 --> 21:30.660
Why don't you have Mr. Bel visit Orphen?

21:30.660 --> 21:33.440
They might find they get along 
if they meet him in person.

21:33.440 --> 21:38.540
Okay! The next time I visit home,
I'll bring my dad back to Orphen.

21:38.540 --> 21:41.440
Then I'll hold a matchmaking party!

21:41.790 --> 21:43.970
Uh, that's not what I meant.

21:43.970 --> 21:46.440
Oh, Ange.

21:49.570 --> 21:51.690
Who should I invite?

21:55.080 --> 21:55.960
It's them.

23:35.060 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.010
<b>"Father and Daughter Meet New People"</b>
